<%
  hero = scene.active_player
  game = scene.game_session
%>
Scene <%= scene.position %> of <%= game.scene_budget %>, <%= scene.part_of_the_story %>, <%= hero.name %>'s turn.

<% if scene.first? %>
This is the opening, as the plan's opening has it.
Show where <%= hero.name %> is and why, and the one or two people <%= hero.name %> meets there, saying who they are.
End on the trouble landing on <%= hero.name %>, so the reader knows what is at stake.
Reveal nothing of what the plan hides, and let no one's look or manner give it away.
<% else %>
<% if (found = game.clues_found).any? %>
Clues found so far: <%= found.to_sentence %>.
<% else %>
No clue found yet.
<% end %>
<% if (marks = game.marks).any? %>
What the rolls have changed so far, and it stays so: <%= marks.join(" / ") %>
<% end %>
<% if scene.clue_overdue? %>
The story cannot wait for clue <%= game.next_clue %> any longer: someone in this scene acts on a want or fear the players have seen.
What they do brings clue <%= game.next_clue %> to where <%= hero.name %> is and shows it plainly, with no mishap or chance behind it.
<% end %>
<% end %>

<% if (clue = scene.clue_in_reach) %>
Clue in reach: <%= clue %>.
<% end %>
<% if scene.last? %>
<% if game.solved? %>
This is the last scene, and the players found what was hidden: the story ends in victory whatever the last roll.
Bring it to the moment they lay what they found before whoever decides; each choice does so its own way.
<% else %>
This is the last scene, and the players won too few of the clues themselves: the story ends in defeat whatever the last roll.
Show plainly why what they know does not settle it; each choice reaches for something still to be saved.
<% end %>
Each choice puts a different thing still at stake on the line, and the roll sets only the price.
The more they won along the way, the easier a choice is; the more they lost, the harder.
<% end %>

<%= hero.name %>, <%= hero.character.identity %>: <%= hero.character.sheet %>.
<% if (companions = scene.companions).any? %>
In the scene with <%= hero.name %>: <%= companions.map { it.character.portrait }.join("; ") %>.
<% end %>
